<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear&nbsp;{!Contact.FirstName},</span></font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Thank you for your interest in graduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU's diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. &nbsp;We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">If you are interested in applying for fall 2017 admission, please first contact the School of Music Admissions office at&nbsp;<a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a>&nbsp;to confirm that your desired program is accepting late applications. If you are interested in future study at ASU, please refer to the information below as a guideline for what to expect when you are ready to apply. For an idea of the course requirements for the various degree programs offered, select one of the checksheets accessible by your degree program of interest&nbsp;<a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/programs/Keyword/music/graduate/false">here</a>.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">Tuition and fees</a> at Arizona State University are reasonable, even for non-resident students. Music Scholarships and teaching assistantships are available. Typical assistantships are 25% which amount to 10 hours or work per week and receive:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Tuition remission covering the non-resident portion of tuition</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">50% reduction in the resident portion of tuition (excluding fees)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">$7,450 stipend for the academic year, distributed over bi-weekly paychecks</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Spoken English requirement</b>: If your native language is not English you must meet <a href="http://learnenglish.asu.edu/international-teaching-assistant">spoken English requirements</a> before you can be considered for &nbsp;teaching assistantship. You may complete the ASU SPEAK test (minimum score of 55).Those wishing to be considered for Graduate Teaching Assistantships should submit a <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-teaching-assistants">TA application</a> by February 15 for an appointment beginning Fall semester.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>A few reminders for <a href="https://students.asu.edu/international/newgradstudents">prospective international graduate students</a></b>:</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">1.&nbsp;If you are from a country whose native language is not English,you must provide proof of English proficiency. Acceptable proof is as follows:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">TOEFL score of at least 550 (PBT) or 80 (iBT)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">IELTS overall band score of at least 6.5 with no band below 6.0</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Pearson Test of English (PTE) score of at least 60</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">It is <i>strongly</i> recommended to complete and pass the English&nbsp;proficiency exam prior to beginning the application process.Scores will be accepted for exams taken up to two years prior to your semester of admission. <b>Applications submitted without a&nbsp;passing TOEFL, IELTS, or PTE score will not be considered&nbsp;for admission</b>. For more information, please visit the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/proficiency">Graduate&nbsp;Education English proficiency website</a>. Another good resource for&nbsp;information on the international student application process is <a href="https://students.asu.edu/international">here</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">2.&nbsp;In addition to University <a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">tuition and fees</a>, international students&nbsp;are required to enroll in the <a href="http://students.asu.edu/healthcoverageoptions">ASU student health insurance plan</a>. <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>More information about this requirement can be found <a href="http://students.asu.edu/internationalstudenthealth">here</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">3.&nbsp;All transcripts and exam scores must be submitted directly to <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/apply">Graduate University Admissions office</a>. To process your&nbsp;application, all <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/apply">international records</a> and official academic credentials must be submitted in the original language <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>accompanied by an official English translation. Translations must <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>be literal, complete versions of the originals and must be translated by a university, government official or official translation service. You cannot do your own translation.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Application Process</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Step 1</b>: You must first submit the Graduate Admissions application, followed by the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music</a> application, before an audition or interview will be scheduled.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Step 2</b>: All transcripts and test scores must be submitted directly to the Graduate Admissions Office of the University.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Step 3</b>: Auditions or Interviews will be scheduled and application materials will be reviewed only after all application materials have been submitted. We are not responsible for application materials sent to the wrong office or directly to faculty. Please check the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate">Graduate Admission site</a>&nbsp;for application information, and the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> for specific application requirements for your degree program.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Applicants to the PhD Music Education, PhD Musicology, and DMA Composition programs</b> must submit GRE scores. The GRE examination in Music is not acceptable for admission to the doctoral program. GRE scores must be from within 5 years prior to the first day of the enrollment term.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Due to the high volume of applicants we receive each year, we recommend that you plan to apply as early as possible.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees" style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Application Deadlines</span></a></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Spring Admission</b>: The application deadline is <b>October 15</b> for all degrees except for the following programs with prescreening requirements:</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All voice concentrations</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Composition</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Composition (Composition, Interdisciplinary Digital Media)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Conducting</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Performance</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The deadline for the above listed programs is <b>October 1</b>.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Fall Admission</b>: The application deadline is <b>December 1</b> for all degrees except for the following programs with rolling deadlines:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Music Education</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">PhD Music Education</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Music Therapy</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Prescreening Materials</b>: Materials uploaded in the School of Music application and must be received by <b>October 1</b> for spring admission and<b> December 1</b> for fall admission. Please visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">our site</a> for more information.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">Audition Dates &amp; Information</a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Spring Admission</b>:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Saturday, November 19, 2016 (flute applicants not accepted for spring admission)</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Fall Admission</b>:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Please review the Graduate <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">audition website</a> for dates specific to your instrument.</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA applicants who are invited to audition after submitting prescreening materials must perform a live, on-campus audition. Recorded auditions are acceptable for master’s degree performance applicants only and must be uploaded <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-recordings-portfolios">online</a> by November 1. CD/DVD audition recordings are not accepted. To be considered for a music scholarship or teaching assistantship, a live, on-campus audition is preferred.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ad hoc auditions may be scheduled with faculty (required for organ applicants), but must be completed by December 1 for Spring admission and February 28 for Fall admission.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Flute applicants are not considered for admission to any spring semester.</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">We welcome you to contact us via email to <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a> if you have any additional questions. We also encourage you to refer to the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/">School of Music Web site</a>&nbsp;as a resource for your admissions questions.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Best wishes,</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Office of Admissions</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">School of Music</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/">music.asu.edu</a> | <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a></font></div><div><font face="arial" color="#ffffff">{!Case.Thread_Id}</font></div></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>